Backport of upstream x87 helper fixes onto our 05/06 x87 patches:
  cf10af6c703d (2026-02-04) target/i386: Fix pseudo-NaN handling in
    FPATAN/FYL2XP1/FYL2X helpers — an invalid encoding (pseudo-NaN) was
    tested after the signaling-NaN test and so silenced as if it were a
    NaN; Intel treats it as an unsupported format (Invalid + default NaN).
  0924d9d3db36 (2026-08-07) target/i386: Clear OF, SF, and AF for
    fcomi/fucomi — the helpers kept the old OF/SF/AF; hardware clears them.
    Applied to the helper (patch 05's x87f_compare shares it) AND to patch
    06's inline compare in x87-shadow.c.inc so the fast and slow paths agree
    (tools/x87-guest-test.py: on/off identical).
9.2.4's floatx80_invalid_encoding() takes no float_status; otherwise the
upstream change verbatim. Skipped on purpose: 57df511180ae / bc40e4fe6263
(FPUS.DE, flush-to-zero after rounding) need the 10.0 softfloat rework
(28f13bccbe6a and the float_flag renames) for a flag no era guest reads.
Drop when the base moves past QEMU 11.1.

